# Files the template-sync workflow must never overwrite in derived repos.
# Everything NOT listed here is treated as template-owned and kept in sync;
# conflicts with local edits surface in the sync PR for review. Files that
# exist only downstream (e.g. your src/ tree) are never touched by sync.
#
# Note: per actions-template-sync, this file itself is not synced — each
# derived repo owns its copy and may extend it with project-divergent paths.

# Replaced per project
README.md

# Customized on day 0 with real owners
.github/CODEOWNERS

# Gains project-specific variables downstream
.env.example

# May be relicensed per project
LICENSE

# ── foundryvtt-docker project-divergent files ─────────────────────────────────
# These intentionally diverge from the template (felddy-fork lineage or merged
# union configs); sync must not propose reverting them.
SECURITY.md
# Records which optional template subsystems this repo uses. Owned downstream —
# syncing it would reset the choices to the template's all-on defaults and
# re-require routing and BMAD, which this repo has deleted.
template.conf
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/dependabot.yml
# MD003/MD029 were retuned to the heading and ordered-list styles this repo's
# documents actually use; the inherited skeleton values matched no file here.
.mdl_config.yaml
# This fork has no root-level language marker, so the ci/ hooks were removed
# and the README rewritten to record why the folder is empty.
scripts/ci/README.md
.dockerignore
# Carries a per-rule allowlist for the upstream felddy maintainer's public
# contact address, which appears all through inherited history (package.json,
# pyproject.toml, Dockerfile, issue templates, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) and is not
# leaked PII. The template has no such entry, so syncing this file strips the
# allowlist and the full-history gitleaks scan in secret-scan.yml starts
# flagging it. Verified against sync PR #59, which proposed exactly that.
.gitleaks.toml
# Private-repo gate ignores for semgrep/container-scan/dependency-review were
# removed 2026-07-05 (repo is public; sync may revert the now-inert gates).
# codeql-analysis.yml stays ignored: this fork scans `actions` and
# `javascript-typescript` only. The upstream image-source Python went with the
# build toolchain, and the routing subsystem took the last .py file with it, so
# a `python` matrix leg fails hard (exit 32, "not any written in Python").
.github/workflows/codeql-analysis.yml
